5

      ⎕TZ←6.2
      ⎕TZ
6.2

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(k)): values too small or too large used
      ⍝ to be silently ignored (⎕TZ left unchanged, no diagnostic at
      ⍝ all) -- unlike a bad type, which already correctly raised
      ⍝ DOMAIN ERROR. No real-world timezone lies outside
      ⍝ [-12 ... 14] hours (UTC-12 to Kiribati's UTC+14), so there is
      ⍝ no sensible value to clamp to (unlike ⎕PP/⎕PW, which clamp an
      ⍝ over-large request to the system's actual capacity); reject
      ⍝ instead.
      ⍝
      ⎕TZ←15
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕TZ←15
      ^  ^

      )MORE
⎕TZ←15: expecting -12 ≤ ⎕TZ ≤ 14 (hours UTC offset)
      )SIC
      ⎕TZ
6.2

      ⎕TZ←14.2
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕TZ←14.2
      ^  ^

      )MORE
⎕TZ←14.199999999999999: expecting -12 ≤ ⎕TZ ≤ 14 (hours UTC offset)
      )SIC
      ⎕TZ
6.2

      ⎕TZ←¯13
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕TZ←¯13
      ^  ^

      )MORE
⎕TZ←¯13: expecting -12 ≤ ⎕TZ ≤ 14 (hours UTC offset)
      )SIC
      ⎕TZ
6.2

      ⎕TZ←¯12.2
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕TZ←¯12.2
      ^  ^

      )MORE
⎕TZ←¯12.199999999999999: expecting -12 ≤ ⎕TZ ≤ 14 (hours UTC offset)
      )SIC
      ⎕TZ
6.2

